module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Flatness.BlowUpSquare.GoodTriple
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# The determinantal ideals of an affine chart under base change

Let `(X, D, M)` be a triple as in Situation 0F8S and let `(U, A, f, M^•)` be an affine chart for
it. For a ring map `A ⟶ B` the base-changed complex `M^• ⊗_A B` is again a bounded complex of
finite free modules, with equation the image of `f`, and its determinantal ideals are the ideals
generated by the images of the determinantal ideals of the chart:
`I_i(M^•, f)·B = I_i(M^• ⊗_A B, f·B)`. In particular principality of the determinantal ideals is
inherited by every base change, which is what makes the good-triple condition stable.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.AffineChart.map_determinantalIdeal`: the
  determinantal ideals of a chart base-change.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.AffineChart`'s
  `isPrincipal_determinantalIdeal_baseChange`: principality of the determinantal ideals is
  inherited by a base change.

## Implementation notes

This is the second assertion of Tag 0F8T, read off the chart's bounded matrix complex: the base
change of the chart is `BoundedComplex.baseChange`, and the identity of determinantal ideals is
Tag 0GSU for that complex and the chart's equation. The first assertion of Tag 0F8T — that the
base-changed complex still represents the restriction of `M`, so that the base-changed data is
again an affine chart — is not proved here, and no statement below presupposes it; it is
`AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.AffineChart.pullback` of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Flatness.BlowUpSquare.ChartPullback`, which imports this file in
order to read off the determinantal ideals of the chart it builds.

The chart's coordinate ring is its ring of sections, so the ring map is a map out of
`Γ(X, U)` and no chosen isomorphism with a spectrum appears.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F8T](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F8T)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GSU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GSU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F8S](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F8S)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory StrictlyPerfect

universe u d

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.AffineChart

variable {S : ComplexAndDivisorSituation.{u, d}}

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0F8T, second assertion.** For an affine chart `(U, A, f, M^•)` and a
ring map `φ : A ⟶ B`, the ideal generated in `B` by the determinantal ideal `I_i(M^•, f)` is the
determinantal ideal `I_i(M^• ⊗_A B, φ f)` of the base-changed chart data. -/
@[stacks 0F8T "the determinantal ideals of an affine chart under base change"]
public theorem map_determinantalIdeal (C : AffineChart S) {B : Type u} [CommRing B]
    (φ : Γ(S.X, C.U) →+* B) (i : ℤ) :
    Ideal.map φ (C.determinantalIdeal i) = idealI (C.complex.baseChange φ) (φ C.f) i :=
  map_idealI_eq_idealI_baseChange φ C.f C.complex i

/-- Principality of a determinantal ideal is inherited by every base change: the image of a
principal ideal is generated by the image of a generator. -/
public theorem isPrincipal_determinantalIdeal_baseChange (C : AffineChart S) {B : Type u}
    [CommRing B] (φ : Γ(S.X, C.U) →+* B) (i : ℤ)
    (h : (C.determinantalIdeal i).IsPrincipal) :
    (idealI (C.complex.baseChange φ) (φ C.f) i).IsPrincipal := by
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := h
  refine ⟨φ a, ?_⟩
  rw [← map_determinantalIdeal C φ i, ha, Ideal.map_span]
  simp

end AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.AffineChart

end
